    "untestable": 0.7,
    "artifact": 0.1,
    "uncertain": 0.05
  },
  "decision": "do_not_proceed",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "The within-team, within-spell rank (or top-vs-other indicator) of the teammate whose pre-absence play-type initiation profile is most similar to the absent player's, compared to all other teammates with sufficient pre-absence minutes, in terms of the change in share of the absent player's primary play types (defined as the two play types the absent player initiated most frequently in the prior 20 games).",
    "unit": "A qualified absence spell: a continuous period of at least 2 games missed by a single non-garbage-time player (min. 15 mpg) who has at least 50 initiations in the prior 20 games, and whose team has at least 3 teammates each playing 15+ mpg in the same prior 20 games.",
    "sample": "All such spells from 2022-23 through 2025-26 regular seasons, yielding ~150 spells (current data only yields 11 cases due to stricter criteria; design would need to relax some criteria or pool more seasons to reach 50+ cases).",
    "power": "A power analysis based on a Wilcoxon signed-rank test (one-sample) against a null median top-gainer probability of 1/k (k=number of eligible teammates) with a realistic effect of 0.35 probability under the alternative would require about 60 spells for 80% power; the current 11 cases provide <25% power.",
