    "falsification": "1) In a set of 'placebo' spells drawn from healthy stretches (no real absence), randomly assign a pseudo-absence and test whether the closest-profile teammate 'gains' more than expected. 2) Test whether the closest-minute teammate, rather than the closest-profile teammate, drives the effect by including both in a joint model.",
    "multiplicity": "Primary analysis uses only the 'initiation profile similarity' metric (cosine similarity or Jensen-Shannon distance) and the top-2 primary play types aggregated. Secondary analyses explore minutes-based and same-position definitions with Holm-Bonferroni correction across the three metrics.",
    "decision_rule": "Compute for each spell the percentile rank of the closest teammate's gain among all eligible teammates. Test whether the median of these percentiles exceeds 0.5 using a one-sample Wilcoxon signed-rank test at α=0.05 two-sided; confirm with a mixed-effects logistic model of top-gainer status.",
    "data_version": "All play-by-play and derived possession data frozen on 2026-11-01; play-type labels from the graph database v.202610; absence spells identified from official injury reports and box-score absences."
  }
}}

